<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fritigern</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 380</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fritigern was a leader of the Thervingi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goths">Goths</a> in the 370s. In 376, fleeing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huns">Huns</a>, his followers were admitted across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a>, but abuse by Roman officials drove them to revolt. He led the Gothic army that destroyed the emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valens">Valens</a> and his army at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-adrianople">Battle of Adrianople</a> in 378.</p></div>
